    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><table class=\"wikitable\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <th>VACUUM SEALS </th> \n   <th>COST </th> \n   <th>UPGRADE POINT COST </th> \n   <th>AVAILABILITY </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>Standard </td> \n   <td>2000 </td> \n   <td>0 </td> \n   <td>Common </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>Improved </td> \n   <td>5000 </td> \n   <td>1 </td> \n   <td>Common </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p>Any Armor can be Upgraded with Vacuum Seals, which include airtight gaskets around all joints and simple <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Life_Support\" title=\"Life Support\">Life Support</a> Equipment that adds 2 kg of weight. This allows the Armor's wearer to survive for 10 hours in the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vacuum\" title=\"Vacuum\">Vacuum</a> of space or any other hostile environment. </p><p><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medium_Armor\" title=\"Medium Armor\">Medium Armor</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Heavy_Armor\" title=\"Heavy Armor\">Heavy Armor</a> can instead Upgrade themselves with Improved Vacuum Seals, which includes enough <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Life_Support\" title=\"Life Support\">Life Support</a> to last up to 24 hours, and adds 10 kg of weight. </p>",
